content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-101 — AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-22120, on the chemically dosed filtered-water line (sodium hypochlorite).",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Dry running: the reported approximately 15-minute dry run exceeds the applicable operating limit. The HF-300 uses Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and the manual states 'never run dry'. The pump is now reported primed and running, but the exposure still requires the planned seal work below.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Vibration: applying Figure 3's HF-300 criterion—mm/s RMS measured on the bearing housings—3.0 mm/s falls in Zone B (2.8–4.5 mm/s RMS, 'Long-term operation'), provided the reported reading was taken on that basis. It is below Zone C at 4.5 mm/s RMS and below the highest severity Zone D at 7.1 mm/s RMS, so it does not trigger the immediate-stop rule.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Temperature: applying the bearing-housing surface-temperature limits, 69 C is within 'normal up to 70 C', 11 C below the 80 C alarm and 21 C below the 90 C trip. The site requirement for a priority-1 work order applies only when temperature is above the manufacturer's alarm limit, so the reported 69 C does not trigger that requirement.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Leakage/seal condition: no leakage has been seen yet, but this does not establish the internal seal condition after the dry run. The manual lists a seal run dry and worn or cracked seal faces among the probable causes of shaft-seal leakage; disassembly and inspection are required to establish actual damage.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Priority/stop decision: plan P2 seal replacement and inspection rather than an immediate shutdown. The dry-run prohibition was breached, but the reported vibration is not in the manufacturer's highest severity zone and the temperature is not above the alarm limit; therefore neither documented immediate-stop/P1 trigger is presently met.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Most likely consequence to investigate first: dry-run damage to the mechanical seal faces, with possible subsequent shaft-seal leakage. Dry running is expressly prohibited and 'seal run dry' is a listed probable cause of seal leakage; actual face wear or cracking remains unconfirmed.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Secondary possibilities only if abnormal vibration develops or persists: the manual lists misalignment, bearing wear, impeller imbalance or damage, and cavitation as causes of high vibration. The current Zone B reading does not by itself confirm any of these conditions.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Before the planned outage, check for shaft-seal leakage and verify vibration as mm/s RMS on the bearing housings and temperature on the bearing-housing surface. Apply Figure 3 and the temperature limits: if vibration enters highest-severity Zone D, stop immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart; if bearing temperature rises above the 80 C alarm limit, escalate to a priority-1 work order within the shift.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C09",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before internal or seal work, electrically isolate and lock out/tag out at the MCC and mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves. Drain and vent first and complete the line-break permit requirements. Use chemical goggles and nitrile gloves because this filtered-water line is dosed with sodium hypochlorite.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the 68 kg back pull-out assembly using certified lifting equipment and a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor. Follow the seal-replacement disassembly sequence: remove the impeller nut and impeller, then withdraw the mechanical seal and shaft sleeve.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C10",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Inspect the removed seal faces and inspect the shaft sleeve for scoring. Replace shaft sleeve HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth. Fit one new HF3-450B cartridge seal; do not fit HF3-450. HF3-450B is pre-set, so no sleeve-setting measurement is needed for seal installation, but the sleeve scoring inspection remains required. Fit a new HF3-120 casing gasket.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Reassemble the pump and tighten fasteners on lightly oiled threads. Use Table 5 values except where superseded by the bulletin: casing bolts M16 to 210 Nm; impeller nut M24 to 160 Nm; disturbed bearing-housing bolts M12 to 85 Nm; and HF3-450B seal gland nuts to 30 Nm, not the superseded 25 Nm value.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After reassembly, perform laser shaft alignment if the work moved the motor or bearing housing. Record and meet the documented tolerances: parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular misalignment 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before returning to service, confirm that the pump is primed and that the Plan 11 flush arrangement from pump discharge is available; never run the pump dry. After restart, inspect for shaft-seal leakage and record vibration and bearing-housing temperature, applying the Zone D stop/notification rule and the above-alarm P1 rule if either is triggered.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C09",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Cartridge mechanical seal, quantity 1. Mandatory replacement selection for this serial-range pump; pre-set and installed without sleeve-setting measurement. Do not substitute HF3-450.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket, quantity 1. Fit a new gasket during seal replacement and whenever the casing is opened.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve, conditional quantity 1: install only if inspection shows scoring deeper than 0.1 mm; otherwise this part is not required.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "For any work inside the pump or on its seal: electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC; mechanical isolation of suction and discharge valves; and a line-break permit, with draining and venting completed first.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For the 68 kg back pull-out lift, which exceeds the site's 25 kg threshold: use a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and certified lifting equipment.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Wear chemical goggles and nitrile gloves for work on this line because P-101 is on the filtered-water system chemically dosed with sodium hypochlorite.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If vibration reaches the manufacturer's highest severity zone, stop the machine immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart. Figure 3 identifies Zone D as 7.1–11.0 mm/s RMS on the displayed range; the reported 3.0 mm/s does not currently activate this control.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If bearing-housing temperature rises above the manufacturer's 80 C alarm limit, raise a priority-1 work order within the shift. The manual also specifies a 90 C trip.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Planned mechanical seal replacement: standard labour allowance 4.0 hours with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Conditional laser alignment: add 1.5 hours with 1 technician if the motor or bearing housing is moved and alignment is therefore required.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal selection conflict: the manual parts table lists component seal HF3-450, while Service Bulletin SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, says not to fit HF3-450 on HF-300 pumps from serial HF3-22000 upward and to use HF3-450B instead. HF3-22120 is within that serial range, so HF3-450B applies; the rule for pumps below HF3-22000 does not apply. The manual's issue date is not supplied, so this decision rests on the bulletin's explicit serial applicability rather than an assumed revision chronology.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Gland-torque conflict: manual procedure 5.2 points to Table 5, which gives 25 Nm for M10 seal gland nuts, whereas SB-2026-014 specifies 30 Nm for HF3-450B. Because this asset uses HF3-450B under the bulletin, apply 30 Nm. Table 5 remains applicable to the other listed fasteners.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Confirm that the reported 3.0 mm/s vibration was an RMS velocity measured on a bearing housing, and record the measurement point; Figure 3's zone classification is documented only on that basis.",
    "Confirm that the reported 69 C was measured on the bearing-housing surface and establish whether temperature and vibration remain stable after repriming; the report supplies no trend.",
    "Actual seal-face condition and shaft-sleeve scoring depth are unknown until disassembly. These findings determine whether the conditional HF3-455 sleeve is needed; the absence of visible leakage does not answer them.",
    "The evidence does not establish why prime was lost during the tank changeover or whether Plan 11 flush remained available throughout the event. Investigate the event sequence and operating controls to prevent recurrence.",
    "No separate labour standard is supplied for inspection-only work, conditional sleeve replacement, or additional repairs discovered on disassembly; revise the labour estimate if the scope expands.",
    "The evidence supplies no numerical post-repair allowable seal-leakage rate or site P2/P3 prioritisation matrix and required completion date; confirm the operational acceptance and scheduling requirements with the responsible engineer."
  ]
}
